        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Following LESS (Xia et al., 2024) we restrict the gradients to the parameters in the LoRA (Hu et al., 2022) adapters and replace the dot product with cosine similarity. Cosine similarity measures gradient directions which are more stable, and avoids over weighting high gradient-norm samples. With  $ \\theta_{L} $ representing the LoRA adapter parameters, we formulate our influence as,",
            "block_bbox": [
                605,
                925,
                1056,
                1143
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
