        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Let  $ \\mathcal{P} = \\{p_i\\}_{i=1}^{N_P} $ and  $ \\mathcal{Q} = \\{q_j\\}_{j=1}^{N_Q} $ denote the pool and query sets, respectively. We collect the ground truth gradients from the pool and query set only through the LoRA parameters and also by masking the prompt as the response-only gradients are more informative. To save on storage, we randomly project the gradients to a smaller dimension using CountSketch (Charikar et al., 2004) projection. We exclude the LM head and the vo",
